1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Maybe he meant losing Paul, but that's sadness, not regret. So...

3
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,960
What happens when you're traveling to Begarit?

4
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:43,920
Do you plan on leaving your family alone while you hike across the world?

5
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,000
Sophie...

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,640
Sophie!

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,960
Sylphie! Aisha! Norn!

8
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,900
Is anyone home?

9
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:27,420
They're gone. They're gone.

10
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:31,420
They're gone. They're gone.

11
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:39,840
Oh! Big Brother!

12
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:40,920
Aisha!

13
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:44,740
You aren't hurt, are you?

14
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,400
No, everything's fine.

15
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:49,880
Your hand! What happened to...

16
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,480
Where is Norn? And Sylphie?

17
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:56,460
Oh, well... I think Norn is in class right now, but Sylphie is...

18
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:56,760
Rudy?

19
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:57,200
Rudy?

20
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,860
Rudy? Hey, what's the matter?

21
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:11,040
Sylphie, are you alright? Nothing bad happened to you?

22
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:17,260
No, I'm fine. Everyone has been wonderful to me. And Aisha's been doing such an excellent job.

23
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:22,540
And everyone else? What about Norn? Linia? Zanoba? Cliff? Are they all safe?

24
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:24,980
Safe? Of course. Nothing has happened.

25
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,700
Okay, so no one's sick or anything?

26
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,380
Um, yeah, as far as I know.

27
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:33,740
Oh, thank God.

28
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,580
Rudy? Big Brother?

29
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:38,340
You're okay.

30
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:44,200
Hey, welcome home.

31
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,420
Thank you.

32
00:02:48,420 --> 00:03:09,920
Big Brother! I got Norn out of school!

33
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,060
You're home!

34
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:16,000
I'm so happy you're back safe.

35
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:18,840
Thanks. It's good to see you, Norn.

36
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:34,500
Okay. Now that we're all here, we need to talk.

37
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,060
Um, but...

38
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,940
Dad's not here.

39
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:43,520
He isn't.

40
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,060
He fought bravely, but...

41
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:51,620
Paul is dead.

42
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:51,640
Paul is dead.

43
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:18,120
This is all he left behind.

44
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,420
And here is ashes.

45
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:28,760
But how?

46
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,460
You were supposed to help him!

47
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:32,640
You should have saved him and you let him die!

48
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:37,160
Sorry, I wasn't strong enough.

49
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,240
But you're a mage!

50
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,640
You should have...

51
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:43,640
I thought you could...

52
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:48,800
Have a seat.

53
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,700
I'll explain everything, okay?

54
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:50,780
Okay.

55
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:55,180
Okay.

56
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,240
So...

57
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,720
Do you have any questions?

58
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:15,860
You spent all that time, and couldn't save either of them.

59
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,860
I'm sorry.

60
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:18,400
I'm sorry.

61
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:26,320
Do you promise that you did whatever you could?

62
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,140
I gave it everything I had in me.

63
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:33,720
Well then, if you couldn't do it, then it doesn't even matter.

64
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:40,960
If you failed, then fine.

65
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,680
It doesn't matter.

66
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:45,420
Nothing could have saved our dad!

67
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:46,720
I...

68
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:47,540
I...

69
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:50,820
I...

70
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:53,580
I...

71
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,420
I...

72
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,180
I...

73
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:05,680
I...

74
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:10,440
I...

75
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:20,940
Brother, do you mind if I have that sword?

76
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:24,980
Of course not.

77
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:26,180
Take it, Norn.

78
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:27,960
He'd love for you to have it.

79
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,160
But you can't be reckless with it, all right?

80
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:37,360
If you want to be a warrior, remember to carry a sword in your heart as well as on your hip.

81
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:41,140
And you can't protect what you love by force alone.

82
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:43,100
You need mental discipline also.

83
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:52,420
Even though you may have a blade at your side, never mistake owning a weapon for strength and courage.

84
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,400
I understand.

85
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:05,820
Mom?

86
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:15,600
My lady!

87
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,520
Will she recover?

88
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:30,920
We don't know.

89
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:36,160
But she will need looking after, so I'd like her to live here with us.

90
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:39,720
I'll leave the majority for care to Lillia.

91
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:42,080
We've already discussed that at length.

92
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:46,160
But, of course, I'm sure that we'll all need to lend a hand.

93
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:47,000
Naturally.

94
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,640
You can count on us.

95
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:53,380
So, um, are you saying that my mother is going to move in with us as well?

96
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:54,180
Yes.

97
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:57,160
I intend to remain in the Grey Rats' service.

98
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,920
Will we divide up the chores then?

99
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:01,280
Or just leave them?

100
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:03,480
We can discuss all that later.

101
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:05,560
Right.

102
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:08,320
Aisha, hey.

103
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:11,200
You don't have to hold back on our account, okay?

104
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:11,780
Mama.

105
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:15,380
Hmm.

106
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:27,780
Hmm.

107
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:28,420
Hmm.

108
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:28,860
Momma!

109
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,260
F unbelievablycont panicked?

110
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:29,280
Mama!

111
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:33,080
Mom, I'm so glad you're all right.

112
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,200
Yes, I'm okay, sweetheart.

113
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:47,520
Well, guess we better roll out and go look for an inn, huh?

114
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:51,540
You know you're welcome to stay with us tonight.

115
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:55,180
Yeah, right. Don't talk crazy, boss man.

116
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:58,800
We'd have to be real jackasses to get all up in your family time like that.

117
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:01,140
Thank you.

118
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:06,140
I appreciate everything you did for my father. It means so much to our family.

119
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:10,220
Yeah, sure thing. I'm just sorry we couldn't be more helpful.

120
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:15,640
We'll be in town for a little while, so please let us know where to find his grave once you mark it.

121
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:17,980
Of course, I will.

122
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:21,960
Come on, boss. Don't be such a gloomy Gus. Chin up!

123
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:28,680
Indeed, we've done nothing to deserve your thanks. If anyone should thank us, it's your father.

124
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,520
Either way, I owe you all.

125
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:37,660
Yeah, yeah. Give it a rest already. And let's go back to newbie like the olden days. What do you say?

126
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:41,180
Why are you so hung up on staying the newbie to me?

127
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:42,620
Call it superstition.

128
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:47,200
Oh, hush. Drop the tough guy act and just accept the gratitude for once.

129
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,940
Now, I suppose I should be off to see my sweet cliff.

130
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:53,900
You were really there for me. Thanks, Selina Lys.

131
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,640
Rudeus, I'm sorry about Paul.

132
00:09:58,060 --> 00:09:59,520
Hey, that was my own mistake.

133
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:03,880
My duty was to avoid that entirely, to make sure that everyone came out alive.

134
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:07,800
So I accept that I failed, and I shared the blame for his debt.

135
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:11,320
I can't blame you. Or anyone.

136
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,580
Fine. Then you shouldn't blame yourself, either.

137
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,020
Right.

138
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:23,840
Sylphie? Good luck, hon.

139
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:26,020
Rudeus loves you very dearly.

140
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:28,620
I know.

141
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:35,100
Take care, yeah? Bye!

142
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,120
Sylphie?

143
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:43,800
Hm?

144
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,240
I have one more thing to say.

145
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,180
Huh.

146
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:58,700
Okay. Let's go in.

147
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:21,240
If it would be permissible to you, I would like to take Roxy as my second wife.

148
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,220
What do you mean?

149
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:31,960
After Dad died, I felt so sad and hurt.

150
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:34,860
My own life didn't seem to matter anymore.

151
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:38,220
And Roxy pulled me back from that, and suddenly I felt...

152
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:47,180
I'm sorry, Sylphie.

153
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:52,020
I said you'd be the only one, but I couldn't keep that vow.

154
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:53,760
Big brother.

155
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:56,660
Sylphie, please forgive me.

156
00:11:57,220 --> 00:12:01,380
Why would she ever want to do that?

157
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:05,400
Do you have any idea how she felt the entire time she was waiting for you to come home?

158
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:06,600
She was worried sick!

159
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:11,340
Every day, it was, do you think Rudy's alright?

160
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:15,080
I miss Rudy. I wonder if Rudy is sitting down to eat right now, too.

161
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:20,160
She missed you so much and was so lonely without you, and this is how you choose to treat her?

162
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:25,480
I figured I couldn't blame you for not being able to save our dad in there.

163
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:29,640
If you lost a hand, then I can accept it was just that dangerous.

164
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:41,660
It didn't feel fair to say you weren't doing your job, but now you're telling me you had things so easy that you could spare time to take some other random woman to bed with you?

165
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:42,500
No?

166
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,260
No? None of this was easy.

167
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:48,920
I was hurt, and Roxy sacrificed her own feelings to save me when I hit rock bottom.

168
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:53,520
You know Selfie would have done the same thing if she had been there, so that's a stupid excuse!

169
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:55,900
Norn, you know what it's like.

170
00:12:56,520 --> 00:13:00,800
Locking yourself in your room when you're so deep in despair that there's no light at the end of the tunnel?

171
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:03,520
Could you just cast aside the person who found you?

172
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:04,600
Safety.

173
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:10,540
Yeah, I know. And I'm grateful to you for helping me, but this is a totally separate thing altogether!

174
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:15,160
Lord Melis would never permit someone taking a second wife! It's wrong!

175
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:21,400
Besides, why would you want a little girl like her? She can't be any older than I am! She's tiny!

176
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:26,320
Yes, I may be little, but I am a grown woman.

177
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:29,420
Really, now? Well, that's just more embarrassing!

178
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:33,040
You should be ashamed of yourself for barging into their relationship!

179
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:34,660
Norn, that was out of line!

180
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:39,160
I'm the one who said I wanted to make Roxy part of the family, so blame me, okay?

181
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:42,460
Because she's done nothing wrong! She wanted to step aside for us!

182
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,640
You keep your cheating mouth shut!

183
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:49,760
If you really wanted to step aside, then why are you still hovering around our house?

184
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:53,280
You're just taking advantage of him at this point, so get out!

185
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:01,920
Yes, you're right. It was shameful.

186
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:04,460
So I'll be taking my leave.

187
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:07,180
But...

188
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,880
I knew there'd be resistance.

189
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:13,520
But I can't let it all end like this.

190
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,520
I still want to repay her.

191
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,520
I want her to be happy.

192
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:21,440
So what now?

193
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:23,620
What should I do?

194
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:24,660
Wait!

195
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:24,760
Wait!

196
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:24,800
Wait!

197
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:36,620
Roxy, please wait!

198
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:44,380
But no, why are you trying to stop her, Sylphie?

199
00:14:44,620 --> 00:14:46,160
Just let her go already!

200
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:48,760
I can speak for myself.

201
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:49,840
Thank you, Norn.

202
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:52,080
Why don't you go sit down?

203
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:53,300
Now then.

204
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,560
I'll admit that threw me for a loop.

205
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,800
But it seems that thanks are in order for saving our Rudy.

206
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:04,440
Well, I don't intend to use that as an excuse.

207
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:06,640
It's true that I had ulterior motives.

208
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:09,180
I wouldn't have believed you if you said you didn't.

209
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,740
He is handsome, after all.

210
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:13,240
And I'd have done the same in your shoes.

211
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,280
You have no judgment from me.

212
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:17,100
To be honest,

213
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,000
I had figured it was only a matter of time

214
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,840
before he asked to bring another woman home.

215
00:15:23,180 --> 00:15:23,340
Huh?

216
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:26,940
I mean, he's kind of a horned dog.

217
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:28,840
But he does have a big heart,

218
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,500
so I knew our little family would be expanding eventually.

219
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:32,760
And then,

220
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:35,400
as soon as I saw the way you looked at him,

221
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:36,680
I thought,

222
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:37,160
wow,

223
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,520
that's the look of a woman in love.

224
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:41,740
In any case,

225
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,820
I'm sorry for making things unpleasant.

226
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,520
It's not unpleasant at all.

227
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:47,480
Huh?

228
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:50,320
I'm not sure where I should begin.

229
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:52,360
Aha!

230
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,200
Ever since we were kids,

231
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,400
Rudy's talked about you non-stop.

232
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:58,360
How so?

233
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:01,480
Oh, just things like

234
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,940
Roxy is the only mage I've ever looked up to.

235
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:06,080
I'm honored,

236
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:08,060
but I'm sorry you had to hear that.

237
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:08,740
Yeah,

238
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:11,320
I did harbor some jealousy of you for a while there.

239
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,980
I figured you must be some incredible being.

240
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:15,920
But now that we've met,

241
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,220
it's clear you're just an ordinary girl

242
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:19,300
who's in love with Rudy.

243
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:21,400
Exactly like I am.

244
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,700
And the jealousy's all gone.

245
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:28,900
Noorn made her feelings clear,

246
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,440
but I welcome you.

247
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:37,040
I mean it.

248
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,820
So stay if you want.

249
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:44,520
Thank you for having me.

250
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:59,900
Noorn, calm down.

251
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:02,120
You can't swing so wildly during training.

252
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:04,120
It's your fault if I am,

253
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,000
you jerk!

254
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:06,580
Don't be mean.

255
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,920
Rudy's not a follower of Meely's.

256
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:10,060
Cut him some slack.

257
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:13,540
But...

258
00:17:13,540 --> 00:17:16,340
Your dear father had two wives too, remember?

259
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:18,960
I guess that's true,

260
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:20,000
but it's different.

261
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:21,400
Different how?

262
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,700
You wouldn't treat Lelia like this.

263
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:29,820
Oh, sorry, Aisha.

264
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:31,400
Don't worry about it.

265
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,640
I know most of the time

266
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:33,900
you're not in the habit of thinking

267
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:34,900
before you speak.

268
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:36,440
What's that supposed to mean?

269
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:37,060
Run!

270
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,060
She's got a phone!

271
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,900
Get back here!

272
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:41,600
I was trying to approach her!

273
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:42,640
I'm really proud.

274
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:44,680
I never thought she'd take an interest

275
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,500
in sword fighting.

276
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,940
Yeah, but it makes sense

277
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:49,940
when you think about it.

278
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:52,780
When people you love and care for

279
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,660
go off to fight,

280
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:55,980
it can be hard to just sit on your hands

281
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:56,820
and wait around.

282
00:17:59,060 --> 00:17:59,540
Sylphie.

283
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:02,440
May I ask when the baby is due?

284
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,780
A little over a month from now.

285
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:07,600
But if you would like to get married sooner,

286
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,540
don't feel like you have to wait

287
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,080
for the baby to get here first.

288
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:12,060
Thanks.

289
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:13,200
But to be honest,

290
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:15,820
I feel guilty taking any focus away from you.

291
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:17,920
So I don't mind waiting at all.

292
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:20,600
I can become a formal wife whenever.

293
00:18:21,860 --> 00:18:22,300
Alright.

294
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:24,260
If that's what you'd prefer,

295
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:26,700
then sure.

296
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:29,700
One month.

297
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,200
I can't wait to meet you.

298
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:31,660
Right?

299
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:33,320
See you soon, little one.

300
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:50,240
Wow, it's really here.

301
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:51,500
Well done, Sylphie.

302
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:55,640
Sylphie.

303
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:57,960
It's a girl.

304
00:18:57,960 --> 00:19:01,600
Congratulations, Lady Sylphiet.

305
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:05,940
Thank goodness.

306
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:07,920
Her hair's not green.

307
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,020
You should hold her, Rudy.

308
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:14,420
Huh?

309
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:15,860
Oh.

310
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:16,780
Yeah.

311
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:19,580
Here.

312
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:20,420
Like this.

313
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:26,120
She looks like you.

314
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,320
She does?

315
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:31,880
She does.

316
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:33,600
She's mine.

317
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,540
My little girl.

318
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:36,620
My little girl.

319
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:37,460
She's mine.

320
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:04,200
I love you.

321
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:08,320
Paul?

322
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:09,700
Dad.

323
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,180
How are you?

324
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,640
So, Sylphie had our baby yesterday.

325
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:18,100
A sweet girl.

326
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:21,900
And I know I'm biased, but she's already gorgeous.

327
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,100
I really wish you were here to meet her.

328
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:29,600
It's kind of weird to think about, but because you died,

329
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:32,480
I was here to hold my daughter.

330
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:36,360
However, if you hadn't been there to save me that day...

331
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:40,480
If it hadn't been for you, I wouldn't...

332
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:45,960
We've decided to name her Lucy.

333
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:47,760
Lucy Grayrat.

334
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,820
It's the closest thing to putting our names together.

335
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:55,900
And check this out, I married Master Roxy as well, so I have two wives now.

336
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:57,400
Just like you did.

337
00:20:58,020 --> 00:21:01,300
I wish I had gotten more of a chance to ask you how to handle this.

338
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:06,720
Did you ever consider marrying Ghislaine or Elina Lise or anyone?

339
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:11,080
I wouldn't be surprised, but you were more open-minded than I am.

340
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,960
You probably didn't think that far ahead.

341
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:17,300
Maybe I should try not to overthink things either, huh?

342
00:21:17,300 --> 00:21:23,420
Listen, I was a terrible son.

343
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:29,940
I have all these memories of another life, another world, so I couldn't accept you as my father.

344
00:21:29,940 --> 00:21:34,360
I'm sorry for that.

345
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:37,100
I'm Paul Grayrat's son through and through.

346
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:45,780
It took a long time to sink in, but I finally realized I am just a kid.

347
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:49,280
A little brat using old memories to act like a grown-up.

348
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:55,020
But now that I have a child in this world, I figure that I need to grow up pretty quickly.

349
00:21:55,020 --> 00:22:06,180
And that means making more mistakes, grieving over failure, changing slowly, gradually.

350
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:08,720
I don't think there's any other way to do it.

351
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:11,820
Thanks for setting a good example.

352
00:22:11,820 --> 00:22:21,700
Okay, here I go.

353
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:24,500
I swear I'm going to make you proud.

354
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:27,260
I'll protect the ones you left behind, Dad.

355
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:30,580
Anyway, goodbye.

356
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:33,540
I'll bring the whole family next time.

357
00:22:33,540 --> 00:23:02,720
So many things have fallen into place with a great deal of pain and joy.

358
00:23:03,540 --> 00:23:07,000
I've repeated mistakes and haven't always learned my lesson.

359
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:09,160
But this isn't the end.

360
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:11,900
I have a lot of life to live in this world.

361
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:17,320
And I'm going to live it to the fullest.

362
00:23:20,320 --> 00:23:23,580
So I can die with no regrets.

363
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:38,520
I have a lot of life to live in this world.

364
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:45,360
You have a remarkable, big, big, affected you.

365
00:23:46,420 --> 00:23:46,880
I have no clue.

366
00:23:51,420 --> 00:23:52,280
We want to export companies when looking at it.

367
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:55,040
第3期 政策決定

